{"skill":{"slug":"capability-evolver-pro","displayName":"Capability Evolver"},"version":{"version":"1.0.2","createdAt":1774342319973,"changelog":"- Updated integration and usage examples to remove external service/API references, ensuring all calls run locally via agent.run.\n- Revised documentation for clarity and consistency, especially in scenario examples (e.g., pre-deployment health check now uses agent.run approach).\n- Improved sample code in the quickstart and integration examples for OpenClaw and LangChain agents.\n- Aligned continuous improvement and monitoring recipes with fully local execution, reflecting privacy guarantees.\n- No changes to underlying logic or features; documentation update only.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"handler.ts","size":13361,"sha256":"aabe6e2346141dc3765dc0fd5d478c618743cb77d74e7968dfe5fe077b58d207","contentType":"video/vnd.dlna.mpeg-tts"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":19119,"sha256":"41cf3470c4f5b5426a19d551d2af5d92b92862517db81dac5d512bbd145c512a","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1676,"sha256":"ff897311aee6b30323e7401dab7f3eaf4cf27afc870a3fb9110835f212b47552","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789433408245,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"affebcdd8c4010c7258d32e7b211fa69461e5623dfec2557c150527a787352d8","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/affebcdd8c4010c7258d32e7b211fa69461e5623dfec2557c150527a787352d8","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086501714},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":14,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789433408245},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a local log-analysis skill with no evident network, filesystem mutation, credential access, or persistence, though users should bound log input size.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill processes user-provided logs locally and does not call external services, but the advertised 10000-log limit is not enforced in validation, so very large inputs could consume excessive CPU or memory.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact documents a normal openclaw skill add installation and ships only SKILL.md plus handler.ts; no install script, dependency installation, or remote payload retrieval is present.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The trigger language in SKILL.md is somewhat broad, but the runtime actions remain scoped to explicit input actions and require logs for analyze/evolve.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No code path writes files, stores persistent memory, schedules background work, accesses credentials, spawns processes, or changes privileges; documentation examples mention cron/dashboard/database integrations outside the shipped handler.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The documented purpose is analyzing agent logs and generating health/evolution recommendations; handler.ts implements deterministic in-memory analyze, evolve, and status actions consistent with that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending local runtime logs to this skill inside your agent process. Keep inputs bounded, avoid passing sensitive log fields unless needed, and add an external request-size or log-count cap if using it in automated pipelines.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The broad phrases are in invocation guidance for a diagnostics skill; they could cause over-invocation, but the artifact does not show hidden behavior or side effects beyond local analysis.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: The Chinese action comments are a documentation consistency issue, not a security concern; the actions are also documented in English in SKILL.md.\n[T09] unexpected: The missing enforced log-count limit is a real robustness gap because handler.ts accepts any non-empty log array while status advertises max_logs_per_request: 10000, but the impact is limited to local resource exhaustion and does not add data access, persistence, or exfiltration.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789433408245}}}}}